    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0486" n="392" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg392"/>

                <head>No. 283.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pendleton to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 21, 1887</date>.
                        (Received July 9.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 459.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, referring to your
                    instruction No. 221 of the 21st ultimo, to transmit herewith a report on the
                    limitation laws of <pb facs="0487" n="393" xml:id="pg393"/> Germany, relating to
                    attachments, fines, and other penalties for the nonperformance of military duty
                    and desertion, which has been prepared by Mr. Coleman, the secretary of this
                    legation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. H.
                    Pendleton.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d283-a1.xml" xpointer="d283-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
